WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>OSHI NO KO</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

01:31.820 --> 01:36.100
<i>If a film creator like me wants to show 
a movie on cinema screens nationwide,</i>

01:36.100 --> 01:38.560
<i>there are several steps 
one needs to go through.</i>

01:39.870 --> 01:43.330
<i>Step 1: Get a movie producer to help.</i>

01:43.330 --> 01:46.200
Okay, time to go scrounge up some money.

01:45.710 --> 01:50.460
<b>Pitch
The 15-Year Lie</b>

01:46.200 --> 01:48.870
I polished the pitch myself.

01:48.870 --> 01:51.960
All you need to do is express 
your passion for the project.

01:52.840 --> 01:55.260
<i>Step 2: Gather investors.</i>

01:55.680 --> 02:00.640
<i>A movie takes around two to three 
hundred million yen to make.</i>

02:00.640 --> 02:04.170
<i>You get a bunch of companies 
to front these production costs,</i>

02:04.170 --> 02:06.460
<i>promising them rights 
and profits in return.</i>

02:06.880 --> 02:09.380
<i>It's what you call 
production by committee.</i>

02:10.320 --> 02:13.780
<i>Step 3: Make your pitch to distributors.</i>

02:14.140 --> 02:17.740
<i>Your distributor's reach will determine 
how many screens your movie can secure.</i>

02:18.310 --> 02:20.620
<i>If you want your film to go big,</i>

02:20.620 --> 02:24.240
<i>you get the most powerful 
distributor you can, but...</i>

02:24.940 --> 02:27.630
Damn it. All the big names said no.

02:27.630 --> 02:31.920
Well, it is based on a delicate subject. 
Major players tend to avoid that.

02:32.420 --> 02:36.500
But some distributors 
do like risky projects like this one,

02:36.500 --> 02:37.730
so let's be patient.

02:40.070 --> 02:42.980
Don't worry. We should get a bite soon.

02:43.390 --> 02:45.940
<i>Kaburagi's a freelance producer.</i>

02:45.940 --> 02:50.690
<b>Pitch</b>

02:45.940 --> 02:50.690
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

02:45.940 --> 02:50.690
<i>He doesn't work for any one distributor, 
so he has to go around pitching projects.</i>

02:50.690 --> 02:55.150
<b>Distributor A</b>

02:51.060 --> 02:54.680
<i>On the plus side, that means 
he can try every distributor out there.</i>

02:51.480 --> 02:55.150
<b>Distributor B</b>

02:52.230 --> 02:55.150
<b>Distributor C</b>

02:52.990 --> 02:55.150
<b>Distributor D</b>

02:55.570 --> 03:00.370
<i>When you're hellbent on releasing a film, 
a man like him becomes real dependable.</i>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Eikyo Headquarters Building II</b>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Members of the Board</b>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Planning Department</b>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Sales Department</b>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Production Department III</b>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Conference Rooms II</b>

02:59.120 --> 03:02.080
<b>Production Department II</b>

03:00.370 --> 03:02.080
The next one's our main target.

03:10.340 --> 03:14.920
Ugh. Everything takes money, money, money.

03:16.140 --> 03:18.420
Would you have preferred 
to make an independent film?

03:18.420 --> 03:20.520
I'm not saying that, but man.

03:21.470 --> 03:22.140
Say...

03:22.780 --> 03:29.020
Nowadays, anyone with a smartphone 
can make films and release them online.

03:29.020 --> 03:31.650
What reason do any of us 
have to stick to theatrical releases?

03:32.020 --> 03:33.360
That's an easy one.

03:33.620 --> 03:37.820
Because that's the only way you can 
become the center of a movement.

03:38.460 --> 03:42.110
You can only kick off a movement 
big enough to be a social phenomenon

03:42.110 --> 03:45.290
with content fueled 
by massive amounts of money.

03:45.570 --> 03:47.580
A social phenomenon, eh?

03:47.580 --> 03:51.900
I never expected the humble Director 
Gotanda to have such lofty ambitions.

03:51.900 --> 03:57.580
Please. Every creator wants their work 
appreciated by more people for longer—

03:57.580 --> 04:01.060
to be something that is 
celebrated a century from now.

04:01.060 --> 04:02.810
You're such an artist.

04:03.430 --> 04:05.590
What can people even say 
a century from now?

04:05.590 --> 04:10.590
Backhanded compliments like, 
"Wow, it actually holds up"? Spare me.

04:11.270 --> 04:14.530
In my eyes, as long as it 
makes money, anything goes.

04:14.820 --> 04:16.530
You greedy money-grubber.

04:18.450 --> 04:21.410
Anyway, our work's not done yet.

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Villain</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Aqua Hoshino</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Confirmed</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Agency President Candidates</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Melt Narushima


Masato Murakami


Yuu Miyashita</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Opening in Schedule


Negotiating w/ Agency


Opening in Schedule</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Theater Actor Candidates</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Takashi Ichikawa</b>

04:21.410 --> 04:23.870
<b>Opening in Schedule</b>

04:21.800 --> 04:23.870
<i>Step 4: Casting.</i>

04:24.220 --> 04:27.330
The main lead can make a difference of 
hundreds of millions in the box office.

04:27.960 --> 04:31.040
Lots of projects live or die 
by who they're able to cast.

04:31.500 --> 04:35.710
But popular actors don't often 
have much room in their schedules,

04:35.710 --> 04:37.250
and they can be picky, too.

04:37.760 --> 04:41.670
I had an actress earmarked 
for the lead role, but she's out.

04:41.670 --> 04:43.140
Something go wrong?

04:43.450 --> 04:48.600
She got pulled at the last second. 
I've heard rumors that she's MIA.

04:49.080 --> 04:51.560
I wonder what happened.

04:52.210 --> 04:57.180
Either way, among all the talent 
I took under my wing and sent jobs to,

04:57.180 --> 05:00.530
I picked out the biggest names right now 
to fill out our prospective cast.

05:00.840 --> 05:03.790
Times like these are 
why I did them all those favors.

05:03.790 --> 05:05.990
It's the culmination of all my work.

05:06.450 --> 05:11.100
Now, how many of them 
will repay those favors?

05:12.020 --> 05:15.260
<i>He constantly networks 
with actors and investors,</i>

05:15.260 --> 05:18.420
<i>knows all the ins and outs of filmmaking,</i>

05:19.010 --> 05:21.570
<i>and oversees and runs entire productions.</i>

05:21.930 --> 05:24.890
<i>He does it all without breaking 
a sweat, but it's really not easy.</i>

05:25.470 --> 05:28.350
<i>He might only ever talk about money,</i>

05:28.900 --> 05:31.810
<i>but nothing he does 
could be done without passion.</i>

05:32.790 --> 05:34.270
Director Gotanda.

05:34.810 --> 05:39.190
I'm genuinely expecting a movie 
capable of sparking a social phenomenon.

05:40.380 --> 05:41.440
If it does that,

05:41.880 --> 05:43.950
I'll make out like a bandit.

05:45.870 --> 05:47.760
Damn greedy money-grubber.

05:45.870 --> 05:48.330
<b>Pitch
The 15-Year Lie</b>

05:49.230 --> 05:50.790
The ultimate choice!

05:51.380 --> 05:52.250
Option one:

05:52.250 --> 05:55.210
Get dropped into a pit full of tarantulas!

05:55.210 --> 05:58.590
Option two: Get shot up by a machine gun!

05:58.590 --> 06:02.840
Option three: Get flattened 
by a falling meteorite!

06:03.180 --> 06:05.140
Which would you pick out of those?

06:05.140 --> 06:06.710
Where did this even come from?

06:06.710 --> 06:09.200
Just answer me.

06:09.200 --> 06:10.810
Okay, option three. The meteorite.

06:11.290 --> 06:13.710
At least I'd die before I felt any pain.

06:15.120 --> 06:18.920
Bzzt! You're a moron if you choose 
anything other than option one!

06:18.920 --> 06:22.490
Tarantula bites can hurt, 
but they're not venomous!

06:22.830 --> 06:24.920
You've got shit for brains, Aqua!

06:24.150 --> 06:25.440
Yeah, I get it.

06:24.920 --> 06:26.960
Well, you've got a shit personality.

06:25.440 --> 06:26.450
I know, right?

06:26.960 --> 06:27.940
Aqua?

06:28.330 --> 06:30.700
As in, Aqua Hoshino?

06:30.700 --> 06:33.330
Yikes! Let's scram!

06:31.640 --> 06:33.330
Is that really him?

06:34.100 --> 06:36.790
Somebody's famous now.

06:36.790 --> 06:41.670
I'll have to think twice before even 
saying your name in public.

06:41.670 --> 06:44.130
Yeah, especially after that story broke.

06:44.920 --> 06:49.480
Just goes to show that Ai's murder 
left a lasting impression on people.

06:51.790 --> 06:53.560
This is a problem, though.

06:53.560 --> 06:55.810
What am I supposed to call you 
when we're out?

06:57.120 --> 06:58.270
Ah-kun.

06:59.730 --> 07:02.050
That should be safe 
to say out in public, right?

07:03.180 --> 07:06.240
What? I'm suggesting it 
for your peace of mind.

07:06.680 --> 07:11.950
We're only here because you protected me, 
so I'll help you out however I can.

07:12.240 --> 07:16.420
But don't get the wrong idea! I'm not 
trying to act like your girlfriend here.

07:17.340 --> 07:20.380
I see you as a dear friend, nothing more.

07:20.700 --> 07:22.040
Huh...

07:22.040 --> 07:24.090
I'd never look at you romantically!

07:24.470 --> 07:27.090
Besides, you have a girlfriend and all.

07:27.090 --> 07:28.840
I broke up with Akane, but okay.

07:31.160 --> 07:32.810
Hmm? Wha?

07:33.650 --> 07:35.110
Oh, okay...

07:35.540 --> 07:37.720
You and Akane Kurokawa split...

07:38.560 --> 07:40.900
<i>Me and my big mouth!</i>

07:40.900 --> 07:44.570
<i>I just had to go and ruin my big chance!</i>

07:45.030 --> 07:46.950
So call me whatever you like.

07:47.240 --> 07:48.030
Huh?

07:51.690 --> 07:54.060
Okay, I've got a recording to get to.

07:54.910 --> 07:56.450
Bye, Ah-kun.

07:56.450 --> 07:57.570
Just get going.

07:58.540 --> 08:00.750
Ah-kun, Ah-kun!

08:02.180 --> 08:03.710
Heh, heh, heh.

08:03.710 --> 08:06.020
Now, isn't that something?

08:06.020 --> 08:10.350
"Ah-kun," she said. 
You two have grown awfully close.

08:10.350 --> 08:11.010
Kinda.

08:11.510 --> 08:15.300
Kana-chan's been in good spirits lately.

08:15.300 --> 08:19.290
I love to see it, personally speaking.

08:19.290 --> 08:21.930
But, well, you know...

08:21.930 --> 08:27.220
I heard from Akane that you two broke up, 
but this is leaving me very conflicted.

08:27.220 --> 08:32.510
It'd help your dear MEMcho out 
a bunch if you handled this tactfully.

08:32.510 --> 08:34.450
You've got nothing to worry about.

08:35.320 --> 08:36.410
I'm done with all that.

08:37.390 --> 08:40.960
I no longer have any wide-eyed illusions 
about leading a happy life.

08:42.210 --> 08:47.350
Uh, it's pretty common 
to feel that way after a breakup,

08:47.350 --> 08:50.730
but everybody has the right to be happy...

08:50.730 --> 08:52.340
That's not what I meant.

08:52.900 --> 08:57.720
It's just more convenient for me 
if I'm on friendly terms with Arima.

09:04.390 --> 09:06.780
<i>I'll use everything I can.</i>

09:08.960 --> 09:12.160
<i>Be it Arima or anyone else.</i>

09:15.530 --> 09:18.000
<b>Aqua Hoshino, Son of Former B-Komachi Idol Ai</b>

09:15.990 --> 09:18.000
<i>The play is already in motion.</i>

09:18.830 --> 09:22.320
<i>Everything's going according to plan.</i>

09:26.140 --> 09:27.040
Ai...

09:27.840 --> 09:32.800
<b>Hoshino Family Grave</b>

09:28.390 --> 09:32.500
I will be the one to make 
your real wish come true.

09:34.760 --> 09:36.220
<b>Hoshino Family Grave</b>

09:35.300 --> 09:36.220
Look at you,

09:36.220 --> 09:38.430
acting like a star-crossed hero,

09:38.850 --> 09:40.380
Aqua Hoshino.

09:41.270 --> 09:42.980
<b>Youtou Private High School
Graduation Ceremony</b>

09:44.940 --> 09:46.400
Senpai!

09:46.400 --> 09:48.410
Congratulations on graduating high school!

09:48.410 --> 09:49.280
Ruby.

09:49.280 --> 09:51.440
Now you can say that's your 
highest level of education!

09:52.620 --> 09:57.960
You keep telling me to go to college, 
but you didn't even apply to any.

09:57.960 --> 10:01.460
My life, my choice. I won't need 
any academic qualifications.

10:01.860 --> 10:06.420
I've made up my mind to live 
and die as an actress in showbiz.

10:06.820 --> 10:11.230
I'll also graduate as an idol after our 
summer concerts and focus on my acting,

10:11.660 --> 10:13.880
using my experience 
with B-Komachi to drive me.

10:14.910 --> 10:16.110
I know.

10:19.310 --> 10:23.040
Graduates are supposed 
to be seen off with a smile.

10:25.100 --> 10:28.650
I think we'll be able to get 
Frill Shiranui to play Ai.

10:29.120 --> 10:33.110
Didn't she only have room in her 
schedule for a supporting role?

10:33.110 --> 10:36.910
Yeah, but apparently 
one of her projects fell through.

10:37.410 --> 10:40.130
A film's main lead is its public face.

10:40.130 --> 10:45.040
Frill-chan has the fame to pull it off, 
and an investor asked for her, too.

10:45.040 --> 10:47.040
I think we should lock her in.

10:58.640 --> 11:00.370
You speak cat?

11:00.370 --> 11:01.600
Whoa, who?!

11:01.860 --> 11:04.310
It's me, Gotanda. Don't you remember me?

11:04.310 --> 11:07.560
Oh, right, the director! It's been ages!

11:07.910 --> 11:11.140
I think the last time we met 
was your fifteenth birthday.

11:11.140 --> 11:12.940
And you gave me 
that video letter from Mom!

11:12.940 --> 11:14.470
Takes me back!

11:13.450 --> 11:16.450
<i>Genetics truly can be cruel.</i>

11:17.070 --> 11:19.910
<i>She's grown up to be so beautiful.</i>

11:20.340 --> 11:23.010
What's up? 
Visiting the agency for something?

11:23.010 --> 11:26.370
Yep. What are you doing out here, though?

11:26.730 --> 11:30.090
Uh, there's someone 
I don't want to see in the office.

11:30.090 --> 11:31.130
You mean Aqua?

11:31.590 --> 11:34.830
I heard you had some kind of falling-out. 
You two still haven't made up?

11:34.830 --> 11:36.100
"Still"?

11:36.880 --> 11:39.550
After how he exposed Mom's secret,

11:39.970 --> 11:41.770
how could I ever forgive him?

11:43.160 --> 11:46.940
Wait, didn't Aqua tell you about the DVD?

11:47.440 --> 11:48.740
What DVD?

11:48.740 --> 11:49.900
Never mind.

11:50.150 --> 11:54.110
<i>Is that obsessive brother planning 
to shoulder it all himself?</i>

11:54.450 --> 11:56.320
<i>How overprotective can he be?</i>

11:57.040 --> 12:01.230
Listen, Aqua had his reasons 
for doing what he did.

12:01.230 --> 12:02.280
Oh, it doesn't matter.

12:02.860 --> 12:06.750
At this point, I don't really 
care <i>why</i> he did it.

12:07.210 --> 12:10.630
It just helped me realize 
you can't trust anyone.

12:11.340 --> 12:14.520
Because everybody's a big liar.

12:20.460 --> 12:21.530
My bad.

12:22.890 --> 12:27.520
<i>Come to think of it, Ai was around 
that age when she had kids.</i>

12:29.140 --> 12:32.480
<i>What set this movie project in motion...</i>

12:32.480 --> 12:34.940
<i>was two DVDs.</i>

12:32.480 --> 12:34.940
<b>To Onii-chan *</b>

12:32.480 --> 12:34.940
<b>Do not open
till you're 15!</b>

12:32.480 --> 12:34.940
<b>To Ruby <3</b>

12:32.480 --> 12:34.940
<b>Open this
when you're 15</b>

12:34.940 --> 12:35.940
Director!

12:36.070 --> 12:37.900
<b>To Onii-chan *</b>

12:36.070 --> 12:37.900
<b>To Ruby <3</b>

12:36.340 --> 12:37.900
Hold on to these for me!

12:37.900 --> 12:39.310
What are they?

12:39.310 --> 12:44.250
Video letters to the future. 
I've been wanting to try this kinda thing!

12:44.250 --> 12:47.340
Give 'em to Aqua and Ruby 
when they turn fifteen.

12:47.340 --> 12:51.040
Of all the silly ideas... 
Just give them the letters yourself.

12:51.340 --> 12:54.270
You know I'd just lose them, right?

12:54.270 --> 12:55.420
Good point.

12:55.910 --> 12:58.510
You're not allowed to peek, okay?

12:58.510 --> 13:00.180
Yeah, yeah.

13:00.180 --> 13:02.010
I'll hand 'em over if I remember.

13:04.090 --> 13:05.430
It's a promise, okay?

13:08.770 --> 13:11.040
<i>I should have given more thought to it.</i>

13:11.510 --> 13:14.830
<i>Why did she address them 
to Aqua and Ruby at fifteen?</i>

13:14.830 --> 13:17.490
<i>Why send them separate DVDs?</i>

13:18.190 --> 13:23.210
<i>Why did Ai leave them with me 
just before she died?</i>

13:23.940 --> 13:26.160
<i>When I figured out the answers,</i>

13:26.080 --> 13:30.040
<b></b>Pitch

13:26.080 --> 13:30.040
<b></b>Title

13:26.080 --> 13:30.040
<b></b>The 15-Year Lie

13:26.080 --> 13:30.040
<b></b>Details

13:26.600 --> 13:29.330
<i>I made up my mind to start this project.</i>

13:30.370 --> 13:33.190
So, who's going to play Ai?

13:33.190 --> 13:37.170
Producer Kaburagi 
wants to go with Frill Shiranui.

13:37.170 --> 13:40.340
Shiranui, huh? She <i>is</i> popular.

13:40.340 --> 13:41.980
But I have another pick...

13:43.320 --> 13:44.720
for Ai's role.

13:45.200 --> 13:47.970
Ruby Hoshino is the one 
I want to play her.

14:03.170 --> 14:06.230
Um, is that what you were looking for?

14:06.700 --> 14:08.970
Have you received formal acting training?

14:08.970 --> 14:12.830
My agency had me take lessons, 
for what it's worth.

14:12.830 --> 14:17.790
I also spend a lot of time around actors, 
so I guess I kinda copied them?

14:18.140 --> 14:20.150
I see. Thank you.

14:20.150 --> 14:21.300
Excuse me.

14:22.650 --> 14:24.600
What did I just get screened for?

14:28.050 --> 14:32.180
This would've been so much easier 
if she couldn't act at all.

14:32.780 --> 14:36.400
Why did you have to go and 
complicate things, Gotanda-kun?

14:36.680 --> 14:39.410
As you saw, Ruby can act.

14:39.410 --> 14:41.930
And we can coach her 
through the finer points as we go.

14:41.930 --> 14:46.060
Casting her as Ai will be truer to life 
and give the film more signif—

14:46.060 --> 14:48.210
That's not the point!

14:48.210 --> 14:51.610
The quality and significance of 
the film are secondary concerns!

14:51.610 --> 14:52.830
Get it through your skull!

14:53.880 --> 14:55.330
Sure, make faces all you want!

14:55.650 --> 14:58.620
But you're a grown man. 
I know you understand this.

14:58.620 --> 15:03.210
What matters most is that we repay 
the companies that invested in us.

15:03.210 --> 15:08.720
<b>Frill Shiranui</b>

15:03.210 --> 15:08.720
<b>Ruby</b>

15:03.640 --> 15:08.720
Casting Frill Shiranui is far likelier 
to put us in the black!

15:09.020 --> 15:11.470
As producer, it's my job to ensure 
a commercial success.

15:11.740 --> 15:14.560
Frill Shiranui is my top pick, 
and I'm not backing down on that!

15:15.330 --> 15:18.120
<i>Producer Kaburagi is totally in the right.</i>

15:18.120 --> 15:23.630
<i>You can't talk about the quality of a 
work until it's a commercial success.</i>

15:24.210 --> 15:27.740
<i>I need this film to be a big hit myself.</i>

15:28.660 --> 15:33.100
<i>This guy once told me, "This isn't 
a place for art. It's a business,"</i>

15:33.100 --> 15:35.860
<i>but I guess that doesn't apply to him?</i>

15:36.640 --> 15:40.640
<i>Well, he </i>is<i> just a big child who 
happens to be able to make movies.</i>

15:41.070 --> 15:42.780
<i>Grow up already, man.</i>

15:43.970 --> 15:46.590
<i>Besides, Ruby's not going to be up for it.</i>

15:47.420 --> 15:51.480
<i>She can't be ready to tell the truth 
about her mother yet.</i>

15:51.810 --> 15:53.520
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

15:55.480 --> 16:00.440
<b></b>I hear they're arguing over the cast
for Director Gotanda's movie lmao

But if they want it to be a hit, they gotta
cast you. Blockbuster name ftw lol

15:56.030 --> 16:00.440
<i>Industry insiders know an awful lot about 
what happens behind closed doors,</i>

16:00.440 --> 16:04.900
<i>and many try to use that information 
to network with talent.</i>

16:05.430 --> 16:08.220
<i>When I hear talk from people like that,</i>

16:08.220 --> 16:11.120
<i>I sometimes start to question how 
I should be playing the game myself.</i>

16:11.620 --> 16:13.080
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

16:16.160 --> 16:16.950
Hey.

16:16.950 --> 16:17.500
Hmm?

16:17.820 --> 16:19.470
Want to grab some crêpes on the way home?

16:19.470 --> 16:21.460
Sounds good! Let's ask Minami—

16:21.460 --> 16:22.460
Ruby.

16:22.820 --> 16:24.960
This has to stay between us.

16:29.040 --> 16:33.050
I wead the scwipt for 
Diwector Gotanda's new film.

16:35.170 --> 16:37.840
I was originally offered a different role,

16:37.840 --> 16:39.500
but my schedule opened up,

16:39.500 --> 16:42.440
and now there's talk of me 
playing the lead instead.

16:42.860 --> 16:45.790
I hear they're still arguing 
about who to pick, though.

16:45.790 --> 16:47.120
Huh...

16:47.590 --> 16:51.570
Huh? Oh, so that's why they 
called me in the other day!

16:51.840 --> 16:53.790
They didn't tell you?

16:53.790 --> 16:58.240
Wait, so you and me 
are gonna audition for the role?

16:59.140 --> 17:00.710
That's not going to happen.

17:01.240 --> 17:06.170
In Japanese showbiz, big stars 
never have to go through auditions.

17:06.170 --> 17:10.130
<b>Star Actors</b>

17:06.800 --> 17:10.130
They only hold them for supporting roles.

17:06.920 --> 17:10.130
<b>Please join the cast!</b>

17:07.670 --> 17:10.130
<b>Hmm, I dunno...</b>

17:10.630 --> 17:14.100
<b>Supporting Actors</b>

17:10.640 --> 17:14.100
The showrunners can't compare 
people on my level.

17:10.880 --> 17:14.100
<b>Please cast me!</b>

17:11.630 --> 17:14.100
<b>Who should I pick...</b>

17:14.930 --> 17:20.000
Offers for starring roles and theme songs 
are generally made one at a time.

17:18.640 --> 17:22.980
<b>Offer</b>

17:18.640 --> 17:22.980
<b>Offer</b>

17:18.640 --> 17:22.980
<b>Actor A</b>

17:18.640 --> 17:22.980
<b>Actor B</b>

17:20.000 --> 17:22.980
Making multiple simultaneous 
offers is seen as unethical.

17:22.980 --> 17:23.980
<b>Actor</b>

17:23.430 --> 17:27.480
Only when the first choice refuses 
do they start negotiating with the second.

17:24.730 --> 17:27.480
<b>Actor</b>

17:24.730 --> 17:27.480
<b>Actor B</b>

17:25.980 --> 17:27.480
<b>Actor C</b>

17:27.820 --> 17:33.240
Actors who get lots of lead role offers 
get to pick and choose.

17:33.690 --> 17:36.240
In other words, I'm interviewing <i>them</i>.

17:37.050 --> 17:40.660
Making big stars audition 
is utterly disrespectful!

17:41.370 --> 17:44.630
At least, that's the view 
of the producers and agents.

17:45.370 --> 17:47.830
It's not like we ourselves 
really see it that way, though.

17:47.830 --> 17:52.510
We'd prefer to be chosen on merit, 
not because of fame or connections.

17:52.510 --> 17:55.350
Top stars have their own stuff 
to worry about, huh?

17:55.350 --> 17:58.850
Yep. I agonize over it, sometimes 
to the point of depression.

17:59.680 --> 18:02.620
It's our job to make quality films,

18:03.270 --> 18:07.320
and yet there are times when 
the quality drops because of us.

18:07.970 --> 18:10.400
Actors should be chosen on merit.

18:10.750 --> 18:12.150
Don't you agree?

18:15.630 --> 18:16.410
I do.

18:16.690 --> 18:17.620
Right?

18:17.980 --> 18:19.260
Let's do just that, then.

18:19.260 --> 18:19.990
Huh?

18:20.340 --> 18:24.490
But didn't you say the showrunners 
can't compare us—

18:24.490 --> 18:27.050
The showrunners can't.

18:27.050 --> 18:29.670
But what if we did it ourselves?

18:30.270 --> 18:33.950
Let's have a showdown, Ruby. 
Whoever loses has to turn down the offer.

18:33.950 --> 18:37.140
That way, the winner 
will get the role by default.

18:37.650 --> 18:38.720
We can call it...

18:39.150 --> 18:40.880
a private audition.

18:42.430 --> 18:44.140
<b>North Exit Shopping Arcade
Hula Dance Club
Private Audition
Sunflower R&R
Yasuoka</b>

18:43.010 --> 18:44.140
Wow.

18:44.420 --> 18:46.600
I didn't know you could 
rent out a place like this.

18:47.050 --> 18:51.710
Broke theater groups and underground 
idols often use them for lessons.

18:51.710 --> 18:56.230
Community centers like this 
have nonsensically cheap rental fees.

18:56.230 --> 18:57.490
Oh? How much?

18:57.850 --> 18:59.380
Two hundred yen for two hours.

18:59.380 --> 19:00.200
Huh?

19:00.200 --> 19:01.740
Two hundred yen for two hours!

19:01.740 --> 19:03.910
That's nonsensically cheap!

19:03.910 --> 19:08.700
It's a government facility built using 
the citizens' blood, sweat, and taxes.

19:08.700 --> 19:11.340
Let's be grateful for the chance 
to squeeze it for all it's worth.

19:11.340 --> 19:14.880
The silent wrath of the highest 
tax bracket! Ooh, scary!

19:15.260 --> 19:18.090
So, what are we doing for this audition?

19:18.630 --> 19:19.800
Could it be...

19:20.100 --> 19:22.000
Huff-puff, huff-puff!

19:22.000 --> 19:23.330
Eep!

19:23.330 --> 19:25.220
Tremble-tremble, panic-panic!

19:25.220 --> 19:26.730
Eek!

19:26.730 --> 19:28.240
Something like that?

19:28.240 --> 19:30.690
Relax. We won't be putting 
our lives on the line.

19:32.400 --> 19:33.860
Sorry to keep you waiting.

19:37.530 --> 19:39.170
Akane-chan.

19:39.170 --> 19:41.990
Good. Now we have all of 
the lead role candidates here.

19:43.120 --> 19:44.940
Long time no see, Ruby-chan.

19:44.940 --> 19:46.210
U-Uh...

19:46.210 --> 19:47.330
Yeah...

19:51.170 --> 19:53.500
<i>Awkward!</i>

19:52.920 --> 19:56.130
<b>Hooked Up On Love for Real</b>

19:52.920 --> 19:56.130
<b>Popular Couple Splits</b>

19:52.920 --> 19:56.130
<b>Popular Couple Splits</b>

19:52.920 --> 19:56.130
<b>Aqua Hoshino</b>

19:52.920 --> 19:56.130
<b>Akane Kurokawa</b>

19:53.500 --> 19:56.130
<i>They just announced
their breakup and everything!</i>

19:56.790 --> 19:59.820
<i>But I did call her my big sis once.</i>

19:59.820 --> 20:01.600
<i>I gotta play it cool!</i>

20:01.600 --> 20:03.870
How's Aqua-kun? Is he doing okay?

20:03.870 --> 20:04.850
Y-Yeah...

20:05.300 --> 20:06.850
<i>Eek!</i>

20:07.130 --> 20:10.390
Shiranui-san, 
what are you playing at here?

20:10.390 --> 20:11.480
What do you mean?

20:11.480 --> 20:16.290
We're the top choices for the lead role 
in Director Gotanda's new film, right?

20:16.790 --> 20:19.860
If you'd let things play out, 
you would've gotten the offer first.

20:19.860 --> 20:25.080
But here you are, making a mess of things. 
So what are you playing at?

20:25.080 --> 20:26.700
Nothing at all.

20:26.700 --> 20:27.760
Liar.

20:30.750 --> 20:33.920
Not very trusting, are you, Kurokawa-san?

20:36.500 --> 20:39.420
Fine. I do have a goal of sorts.

20:39.420 --> 20:41.050
What is it?

20:41.050 --> 20:41.930
That's a secret.

20:42.750 --> 20:45.890
That said, the reason 
I proposed this private audition

20:46.370 --> 20:50.850
is ninety percent because I want 
to feel good about doing my job.

20:51.470 --> 20:56.820
I want to go into it thinking, 
"I really was the best fit for this role."

20:56.820 --> 21:00.580
Not my problem. This is the 
first day off I've had in ages.

21:00.580 --> 21:02.300
If that's all this is, I'm out of here.

21:02.300 --> 21:04.260
We'll be acting opposite Aqua-san.

21:04.780 --> 21:06.040
Aqua?

21:07.550 --> 21:09.290
You say this is an audition.

21:09.780 --> 21:11.500
Who's judging it?

21:11.770 --> 21:15.760
It's between us. We'll decide the winner.

21:16.240 --> 21:17.870
What's the litmus test?

21:17.870 --> 21:20.470
Why don't we just play the part?

21:20.470 --> 21:24.430
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

21:20.910 --> 21:24.430
I haven't gotten the script. 
I don't know what the part even is.

21:24.430 --> 21:26.260
Me neither.

21:26.260 --> 21:27.800
Oh, right.

21:27.800 --> 21:32.400
I can't really show the script to people 
who haven't gotten an offer yet...

21:32.790 --> 21:37.360
Hmm... In that case, 
how about I pick a theme,

21:37.360 --> 21:40.420
and we each improvise a scene on that?

21:40.420 --> 21:41.520
Fine by me.

21:41.520 --> 21:42.320
Yep.

21:42.600 --> 21:44.050
Okay, let's go with that.

21:44.050 --> 21:45.070
The theme is...

21:45.070 --> 21:46.280
<b>Lie</b>

21:46.660 --> 21:47.790
"Liar."

21:50.420 --> 21:54.420
I'll go first. Use the time 
to think about what you'll do.

21:56.120 --> 21:58.560
First up, here is Frill Shiranui,

21:58.560 --> 21:59.940
with "Liar."

22:02.470 --> 22:05.680
Awoo!

22:06.430 --> 22:08.500
Wolf!

22:08.500 --> 22:10.750
Wolf!

22:10.750 --> 22:13.080
Wolf!

22:14.250 --> 22:18.270
Tch, not a damn soul believes me anymore.

22:18.900 --> 22:21.400
I wish they'd give me attention.

22:22.090 --> 22:23.680
I'm so lonely...

22:29.290 --> 22:31.750
What the hell should I do?

22:34.980 --> 22:39.950
I know! Maybe they'll give me 
attention if I tell the truth?

22:40.590 --> 22:43.170
No wolf!

22:43.620 --> 22:47.920
And then men from all over the village 
showed up with their hunting rifles

22:47.920 --> 22:52.390
and raked the boy 
who cried wolf over the coals.

22:52.730 --> 22:54.030
Fin.

22:55.040 --> 22:55.900
Huh?

22:55.900 --> 22:56.850
A skit?

22:57.250 --> 23:00.420
Oops, my comedian side shone through.

23:00.420 --> 23:04.320
You two don't need punchlines, okay? 
Do whatever you like.

23:04.740 --> 23:08.570
So yeah, I can act a bit.

23:08.570 --> 23:10.540
Not as much as Kurokawa-san, of course.

23:11.300 --> 23:14.660
But I do have a sort of appeal 
that only I can bring to a role,

23:14.660 --> 23:17.000
so I'd like you to take that into account.

23:17.420 --> 23:21.080
<i>Being good at acting isn't the only 
thing that makes a good actor.</i>

23:21.460 --> 23:26.430
<i>She has an air about her that draws 
the eyes of one and all to herself.</i>

23:26.910 --> 23:29.800
<i>That's a powerful asset for any actor.</i>

23:29.800 --> 23:32.070
Okay, your turn next, Ruby.

23:33.320 --> 23:37.520
<i>If this were any other audition, 
Ruby-chan wouldn't stand a chance.</i>

23:37.820 --> 23:40.520
<i>So there must be a reason 
she's a part of this,</i>

23:41.110 --> 23:43.940
<i>and I'm betting it has to do 
with this role—this movie.</i>

23:44.510 --> 23:45.600
Say, Ruby.

23:45.900 --> 23:49.760
What does lying mean to you?

23:56.620 --> 24:00.000
<b>Episode 33










Greed and Passion</b>

